  "title": "Knot meets knot only pairwise in the knot's spaces",
  "subject": "Whether two parts of a knot's space can meet knot to knot, without a hub, across three or more channels",
  "conclusion": "A knot's space stays non-colourable under a twist pattern exactly when the pattern is a cocycle of its incidence graph (sign-nonsingularity and the uniqueness of Pfaffian signings up to switching). Hence if both sides of a nontrivial cut accept knots on its channels, the cut has exactly two edges: knot meets knot only as two-place parity, and three-place emergence never passes between parts without a hub.",
